// Per-machine build settings. Committed, and empty of values on purpose.
//
// `project.yml` points both shipping targets at this file. xcodegen validates every
// `configFiles` path and fails the whole generate if one is missing, so this file has
// to exist in a fresh checkout — which is why it is committed rather than ignored.
//
// It holds no settings itself. The one setting that differs per machine is
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM, and that lives in `Local.override.xcconfig`, which is gitignored.
// The `?` in `#include?` means "include it if it is there": with no override file this
// line resolves to nothing, DEVELOPMENT_TEAM stays unset, and the build is exactly what
// CI builds — simulator tests and `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`, no team, no signing.
//
// To sign for a real device, or to run `scripts/release.sh`:
//
//     cp Roost/Config/Local.override.xcconfig.example Roost/Config/Local.override.xcconfig
//     $EDITOR Roost/Config/Local.override.xcconfig        # paste the Team ID
//
// No Team ID is ever committed. See `docs/RELEASE.md`.

#include? "Local.override.xcconfig"
